eloop: use ppoll(2) on QNX, which has no kqueue.

eloop.c uses kqueue(2) whenever BSD is defined. QNX defines BSD for its
FreeBSD network stack (previous patch) but has no kqueue (no <sys/event.h>);
it has ppoll(2), dhcpcd's portable backend. Take that on QNX.

Upstream-Status: QNX-specific

--- a/src/eloop.c
+++ b/src/eloop.c
@@ -36,7 +36,7 @@
  * On Linux use epoll(7)
  * Everywhere else use ppoll(2)
  */
-#if defined(BSD) || defined(__APPLE__)
+#if (defined(BSD) || defined(__APPLE__)) && !defined(__QNX__)
 #include <sys/event.h>
 #define USE_KQUEUE
 #if defined(__NetBSD__)
